{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Research round 3 complete (2026-07-29) — evidence for the conditional items:\n\nCLARITY BACKTEST (n=153 tickets, 7 days; 104 passed-plan FP set / 55 blocked-plan hit set, descriptions reconstructed as-of-review): R1 verification-presence floor PROMOTE TO BLOCKING (1-4/104 marginal FP beyond existing P1; 4/4 hits overlapped real blocking findings). R2 vague-lexicon-in-AC: advisory until P6 lexicon regex fixed (\\bclean matches 'cleanly'/'clean pass' — 6/8 FPs; add trailing \\b, contextualize 'clean'), then re-test at ~1-2% FP. R3 spec-by-example/R4 riskiest-assumption/R5 compound-AC REJECTED as blockers: fire at near-identical rates on good vs blocked plans (76/71%, 86/80%, 51/60%) — no discrimination; belongs in guide/coaching.\n\nT5c/T10 DEMOTION: RESOLVED NO. Zero-blocking is a CONFIG artifact (all five never-blocking criteria carry blocking_enabled:false, threshold 0.95) not a quality signal. Codebase grounding of strong findings: T10 62%, T5c 46% cite concrete repo artifacts (.tf lines, fetch-secrets.sh, network.tf). Tool use per criterion is NOT recorded — add instrumentation (persist per-call request_count/usage into checkpoint+sidecar), but finding-content evidence already shows tools inform findings. OSS survey unanimous: no maintained LLM security reviewer works without repo grounding (Anthropic action mandates repo-context phase + exploitability-proof pass; Semgrep 'exploitability depends on context'; CodeRabbit clones whole repo). T5c 'AS WRITTEN' rubric = confirmed bug; rewrite toward grounded exploitability, keep AGENT. T10 cannot justify skipping IaC state; keep AGENT.\n\nNEVER-BLOCKING FIVE (per-criterion verdicts from ~105 hand-read findings): T3 = calibration, best of five (13/20 class-a, e.g. nonexistent pydantic-ai-slim[retries] extra) → enable blocking @0.85-0.90, no other change. T10 = calibration → blocking @0.90 MAJOR classes + adopt augmented DET gate incl. GHA tokens (28% fire, 100% strong-finding recall). T11 = YIELD problem: post-rollback rubric paragraph is a stock-finding generator (8/21 samples near-identical tautologies vs append-only store) → tighten rubric (fire only on changed interpretation of persisted records; 1-per-plan cap), advisory except demonstrated-data-loss @>=0.9. T5c = NO DET GATE (best keyword gate fires 66% AND misses 5/67 strong findings that are unambiguously real — security findings live in plans without security words); rubric dedup + evidence requirement + blocking @0.90 HIGH classes. G7 = strongest blocking case (11/22 class-a contract contradictions) → blocking for contradicts_reality @0.80-0.85; unresolvable parent → abstain not finding; closed-parent rule.\n\nZERO-FINDING FOUR — validated DET triggers (regexes in agent report; measured over all 2,705 review-time descriptions): T13 71.0% fire (29% skip), T14 41.8% (58% skip — biggest win), removal-rationale 69.8% (+ file_impact-deletion OR), asserted-capability 75.0% (conjunction module-ref AND capability-verb). Zero recall to lose; conservative by design; implement as _DET_OVERLAY_RULES entries.\n\nMID-REVIEW CANCEL: SAFE with own-material-only predicate. Sign-time generation equality already excludes tracker HEAD + relation snapshot (7c3c08df8/d70a: store-wide equality aborted signing on unrelated writes) — HEAD-keyed cancel would reintroduce d70a. Design: attest.current_material_fingerprint probe under local_read_context at 2 between-pass seams (post-finders, pre-coach), threading.Event checked in pass1._chunk, claimability.indeterminate_verdict('cancelled-stale'), no sidecar, exit 2. Checkpoints keyed by material fingerprint = already orphaned after edit (zero partial credit). Do NOT cancel on related_material (discards reusable checkpoints; sign-time catches it).\n\nSPLIT-BRAIN: understood, both sides correct. Pin = bug fix ec85e4cd5 (agent ticket tools resolved store under code snapshot lacking .tickets-tracker; 26 show_ticket errors → INDETERMINATE); live-local fingerprint load-bearing (must re-validate under live store write lock; pinned-copy fingerprint would never go stale). Residual: locally-edited-unpushed CHILD reviewed old-text by agent / new-text by DET+pins, signature binds new; nothing detects skew. Action: document divergence + add skew detection, do NOT unify roots.\n\nVERBS: claim already fails closed, exit 1, actionable message (gates.py:209-217) — confirmed. edit --review: RECOMMEND, ship first (edit mutates exactly the fingerprinted fields; single process makes ordering unskippable; complements cancel — same own_material helper). claim --review second (hook at claim.py:133; accept ms-scale fail-closed TOCTOU; do NOT propagate through parent cascade). Both foreground, CLI-only, documented non-atomic vs reconverge.\n\nPRICING: genai-prices primary (MIT, pydantic vendor alignment — pydantic-ai RequestUsage implements its AbstractUsage; cache read/write tiers; historical prices by timestamp; bundled offline data; typed LookupError → honest 'cost unavailable' incl. fake runner). Repo-local overlay JSON (litellm field vocabulary) for brand-new models. Extend usage_log rows with model/provider/UTC timestamp; label column 'est. cost'.\n\nCOACH PARITY: confirmed bug — guide is criterion-complete, move-blind (zero of 15 moves named; no rebar explain <move>). Top-5 gap (360 field hits): spec-by-example 150, observable-proxy half of plan-the-verification 96, riskiest-assumption 51, [operator-attested] tag 41, propagate-to-children 22. Fix: 'Responding to coaching moves' section keyed by move name, frequency-ordered.\n\nDOCS REVIEWER: structural dead end — docs-only findings have NO path to surface (nit_suppressed + blocking_enabled:false); 47/125 nit-suppressed had validity>=0.8 AND impact>0. Both fixes: (1) impact-aware nit suppression (suppress only impact==0) at workflow_ops.py:443-446; (2) rubric forbids absence speculation (95 absence-refuted drops = correctly rejected but billed).\n\nTTL: RECOMMEND STAYING AT 5 MIN. Refresh-on-hit + measured inter-pass gaps ~50-100ms mean the 5-min window covers the entire review (87% of reviews >5min total but no gap approaches 5min). 1h premium buys nothing cross-review (revise loops change prefix bytes). Investment → approved plan-first prefix restructure. Secondary: gate runs use MemoryRecorder, per-step durations discarded — persist if pass timing matters."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785378396864103001,"uuid":"1a118d90-52e4-4f73-8bb5-51fa08bbe226"}